  "officialHtml": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-sw1000.html",
  "prefLabel": "Env-Sw 1005.08 Financial Assurance",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-Sw 1005.08 Financial Assurance.\n\n(a) The permittee shall be responsible for the cost of facility closure, including all post-closure obligations.\n\n(b) Prior to commencing operation of a facility, the permittee shall assure that adequate funds, in an amount no less than the amount calculated pursuant to Env-Sw 1403.02, are readily available to cover the cost of facility closure.\n\n(c) The permittee shall provide a formal financial assurance plan when required pursuant to Env-Sw 1400.\n\nSource. #6619-B, eff 10-29-97; (See Revision Note at chapter heading for Env-Sw 1000); ss by #8459, eff 10-28-05 (formerly Env-Wm 2705.08); ss by #10598, eff 7-1-14; ss by #13864, eff 2-6-24",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-sw1000.html"
